        "math_academy_id": "q-5543",
        "problem": "Given that $n\\ge 2$ is an integer, simplify $\\frac{(n-2)!}{n!}.$",
        "worked_solution": "First, notice the following:\n\n$$\nn!=n\\cdot (n-1)\\cdot (n-2)!\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel the $(n-2)!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(n-2)!}{n!} & =\\frac{(n-2)!}{n\\cdot (n-1)\\cdot (n-2)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(n-2)!}}{n\\cdot (n-1)\\cdot \\cancel{(n-2)!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n(n-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
